<TopicLayout slug="heaven/first-and-foremost" noImage>
  <!--<p class="lede"><b>First and Foremost</b></p>-->
  <div class="verse-callout">
    <p>" Whom have I in heaven but you?..." - Psalms 73:25</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    If God wasn't in heaven, would you want to be there? Be honest! If we saw clearly
    heaven would have nothing for us without our Lord. He is the One who completes
    us and fulfills us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without Jesus Heaven would only be a lovely place without the Lover, and what is a honeymoon without the spouse?
  </p>
  <p>
    This is how it should be for us. What does heaven have for us if it does not have Him?
  </p>
  <p>
    Consider this John Piper quote: "People who would be happy in heaven if Christ
    were not there, will not be there. The gospel is not a way to get people to heaven;
    it is the way to get people to God."
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      "I keep my eyes always on the Lord . With him at my right hand, I will not be shaken. Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will rest secure, because you will not abandon me to the realm of the dead, nor will you let your faithful one see decay. You make known to me the path of life; you will fill me with joy in your presence, with eternal pleasures at your right hand." - Psalms 16:8-11
      <br>
      "Surely you have granted him unending blessings and made him glad with the joy of your presence." - Psalms 21:6
      <br>
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: It is in God's presence that we find joy.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      "As for me, I will be vindicated and will see your face; when I awake, I will be satisfied with seeing your likeness." - Psalms 17:15
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: Our souls satisfaction lies in seeing the likeness of God.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      "I have seen you in the sanctuary and beheld your power and your glory. Because your love is better than life, my lips will glorify you." - Psalms 63:2-3
      <br>
      Meditation: King David saw God in His sanctuary. He beheld His power and glory. Yet, David's greatest takeaway from that incredible experience was the love of God, a love David realized was better than life itself. Maybe your seeking that kind of love, a love that makes life worth living. Seek it in God for in Him alone it resides.
    </li>
    <li>
      "The Lord is my shepherd, I lack nothing. He makes me lie down in green pastures, he leads me beside quiet waters, he refreshes my soul. He guides me along the right paths for his name’s sake." - Psalms 23:1-3
      <br>
      Meditation: "He refreshes my soul." Not vacation, or Yoga, or relationship, or bottle, or vape, but God Himself refreshes our soul.
    </li>
    <li>
      “...The body is not meant for sexual immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body." - 1 Corinthians 6:13
      <br>
      Meditation: You can fulfill your earthly desires but your earthly desires will never fulfill you, that is because you were meant for Lord and the Lord is meant for you.
    </li>
  </ul>
</TopicLayout>

